{
  "rationale": "This is the final iteration, so the design raced here is the last development evidence and the basis for the unseen-track race. Iteration 9 (y=0.045, ±0.055, 16 mm, 0.12 m track, 0.035 m wheels, 0.6 kg, base_speed 1.4) is the best measured geometry at 67.70. Its oval mean was 102.7 and its slalom progress 0.100. Iteration 10 (y=0.05, ±0.06) lost fewer line events on s-bend (0 vs 0.9) but scored lower at 60.5, mainly on oval (mean 78.1 vs 102.7, with a wide spread of 52 to 133). Its slalom still lost the line once. Its controller is unknown to me, so I cannot say whether its gains were tuned for it. Across all 11 iterations the oval max_error has stayed at 0.060 to 0.063 under every geometry change, and only the forward row and the outer span have moved progress on the bends. Because the Integrator tuned its controller on the iteration 9 geometry, and that geometry gave the best total score, I return to it exactly. Changing geometry on the last iteration would add untested risk to the unseen-track race. The sensor layout is unchanged: five 16 mm sensors at y=0.045 with x = -0.055, -0.0275, 0, 0.0275 and 0.055.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.055, "y": 0.045},
      {"x": -0.0275, "y": 0.045},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.045},
      {"x": 0.0275, "y": 0.045},
      {"x": 0.055, "y": 0.045}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.035,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.6
  },
  "intent": "Return to the iteration 9 geometry exactly, which scored best (67.70), so the Integrator's controller is matched to the layout it was tuned on. The forward row at y=0.045 with ±0.055 outer sensors is the best measured trade-off so far. Expected: line losses near 0.9 to 1.0 per trial on s-bend and slalom, s-bend progress near 0.14, and oval progress near 0.24. This is a hold, not a new test, because the final race should be the most reliable design available.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "integration_feedback": "State whether the controller held with this geometry unchanged, and whether any controller change you made was needed for the geometry. Report line_loss_events on s-bend and slalom, and progress on each track against the iteration 9 values (oval 0.242, s-bend 0.1425, slalom 0.100). Say whether any gain or line_loss choice would lower the line losses at this row, since that is the last lever left for this layout.",
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "control_effort", "controller_errors", "noise_robustness"]
  },
  "learning": "Across iterations 0 to 10, the oval max_error floor (0.060 to 0.063) did not move under any geometry change. Forward-row position and outer span changed bend progress and line losses, but not the floor. The best measured geometry is iteration 9's layout, and this iteration holds it for the final race. Whatever the race shows about line losses on the curves is the main evidence for future work, not further geometry changes.",
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Hold best layout (y0.045)",
      "notes": "Returns to the iteration 9 geometry (y=0.045, ±0.055 span, 16 mm sensors, 0.12 m track), the best measured score at 67.70, so the Integrator's tuned controller stays matched. Iteration 10 raised bend progress but scored lower, so it was not kept."
    }
  }
}
